  "id": "evaluation-apprehension",
  "term": "evaluation apprehension",
  "definition": "Evaluation apprehension is worry or fear about being judged negatively by others. In idea-generation settings, it can make people less willing to share unconventional or risky ideas, and anonymity is often described as a way to reduce it.",
